1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
What’s new in Island Time 1.25.0, shown with mock game data.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,000
Playing a downloaded copy? When a newer version is out, the game tells you when it starts.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,500
Download it, ask again later, or skip that version. You can turn this off in Settings.

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,000
The Windows app now opens the latest version whenever you’re online, so you don’t need to reinstall.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,500
The first time, your saved games, name and settings come along. Offline, its own copy updates itself.

6
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:27,000
Each saved game on the start page now has a delete button beside Continue.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,500
Tap it to delete that game.

8
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:36,000
It always asks first, because a deleted game can’t be brought back.

9
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,500
To keep a copy, use Transfer a saved game in the Menu first.

10
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:46,000
Play free in your browser at krazow.github.io/islandtime

